#### Manual Service Mapping Conversion Plan
- Current manual mapping scope:
  - `AuthService.MapToAuthResponse(User user)` manually creates `AuthResponse`.
  - `RegisterAsync`, `LoginAsync`, and `GetCurrentUserAsync` call `MapToAuthResponse`.
- Add a dedicated AutoMapper profile in `MangaManagementSystem.Business/Mappers/Profiles/UserProfile.cs`.
- Configure `CreateMap<User, AuthResponse>()` and explicitly map:
  - `RoleName` from `User.Role.RoleName`.
  - Direct properties (`UserId`, `UserName`, `Email`, `DisplayName`) by convention.
- Inject `IMapper` into `AuthService`.
- Replace each `MapToAuthResponse(...)` call with `_mapper.Map<AuthResponse>(...)`.
- Remove the private `MapToAuthResponse` method after all callers are replaced.
- Keep entity creation in `RegisterAsync` manual; AutoMapper should only replace entity-to-response mapping, not password hashing, token generation, or database update logic.
- Verify every mapped `User` query includes `.Include(x => x.Role)` before mapping so `RoleName` is available.
- Confirm `services.AddAutoMapper(typeof(DependencyInjection))` discovers the new profile through the Business assembly.

#### [MODIFY] [AuthService.cs](file:///d:/Class/SU26/PRN232/CODE/MangaManagementSystem/MangaManagementSystem.Business/Services/Implements/AuthService.cs)
- Inject `IMapper` into the constructor.
- Remove the manual `MapToAuthResponse(User user)` method.
- Replace all instances of manual mapping with `_mapper.Map<AuthResponse>(user)`.

### 2. Controller Refactoring

#### [MODIFY] [AuthController.cs](file:///d:/Class/SU26/PRN232/CODE/MangaManagementSystem/MangaManagementSystem.WebApi/Controllers/AuthController.cs)
- Change all method return types from `Task<ActionResult<ApiResponse<T>>>` to `Task<IActionResult>`.
- Update `[ProducesResponseType]` attributes to use `typeof(BaseResponse)`.
